<div class="sandbox-container my-12 p-6 border border-ink-faint bg-surface rounded-lg select-none transition-colors duration-300">
  <div class="sandbox-meta flex justify-between items-center mb-4 border-b border-ink-faint pb-3 flex-wrap gap-2">
    <span class="sandbox-title font-garamond text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.15em] uppercase text-accent font-medium">Twin-Network Counterfactual Simulator</span>
    <span class="sandbox-instructions text-[0.7rem] text-ink-dim italic">Adjust the sliders to observe the abduction, action, and prediction phases in real-time</span>
  </div>
  
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-4">
    <!-- Left panel: Causal Inputs -->
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-5 bg-[#09090a] p-5 rounded border border-white/5">
      <div>
        <label for="confounder-x" class="block text-[0.7rem] font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-ink-dim mb-1">
          Environmental Visibility (Confounder X) = <span id="val-x" class="text-accent font-bold">0.50</span>
        </label>
        <input 
          type="range" 
          id="confounder-x" 
          min="-2.0" 
          max="2.0" 
          step="0.1" 
          value="0.5" 
          class="w-full h-1 bg-white/10 rounded-lg appearance-none cursor-pointer accent-accent"
        />
        <div class="flex justify-between text-[0.6rem] font-mono text-ink-dim mt-1">
          <span>Dark / Low Contrast (-2.0)</span>
          <span>Clear / Daylight (2.0)</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="border-t border-white/5 pt-3">
        <label for="factual-t" class="block text-[0.7rem] font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-ink-dim mb-1">
          Factual Deceleration Force (Treatment T*) = <span id="val-t" class="text-amber-500 font-bold">-1.00</span>
        </label>
        <input 
          type="range" 
          id="factual-t" 
          min="-2.0" 
          max="2.0" 
          step="0.1" 
          value="-1.0" 
          class="w-full h-1 bg-white/10 rounded-lg appearance-none cursor-pointer accent-accent"
        />
        <div class="flex justify-between text-[0.6rem] font-mono text-ink-dim mt-1">
          <span>Swerved / Delayed Braking (-2.0)</span>
          <span>Maximum Braking (2.0)</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="border-t border-white/5 pt-3">
        <label for="exogenous-uy" class="block text-[0.7rem] font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-ink-dim mb-1">
          Passenger Resilience (Exogenous Noise U_Y) = <span id="val-uy" class="text-stone-400 font-bold">-0.37</span>
        </label>
        <input 
          type="range" 
          id="exogenous-uy" 
          min="-2.0" 
          max="2.0" 
          step="0.1" 
          value="-0.4" 
          class="w-full h-1 bg-white/10 rounded-lg appearance-none cursor-pointer accent-accent"
        />
        <div class="flex justify-between text-[0.6rem] font-mono text-ink-dim mt-1">
          <span>Frail / Poor Angle (-2.0)</span>
          <span>Robust / Safety Cage (2.0)</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="border-t border-white/5 pt-3">
        <label for="counterfactual-tc" class="block text-[0.7rem] font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-ink-dim mb-1">
          Counterfactual Deceleration (Intervention do(T) = x) = <span id="val-tc" class="text-emerald-500 font-bold">1.00</span>
        </label>
        <input 
          type="range" 
          id="counterfactual-tc" 
          min="-2.0" 
          max="2.0" 
          step="0.1" 
          value="1.0" 
          class="w-full h-1 bg-white/10 rounded-lg appearance-none cursor-pointer accent-accent"
        />
        <div class="flex justify-between text-[0.6rem] font-mono text-ink-dim mt-1">
          <span>Swerved / Delayed Braking (-2.0)</span>
          <span>Maximum Braking (2.0)</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    
    <!-- Right panel: Factual vs Counterfactual Worlds -->
    <div class="flex flex-col bg-[#09090a] p-5 rounded border border-white/5 justify-between gap-4">
      <div>
        <h4 class="text-[0.7rem] font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-ink-dim mb-3 border-b border-dashed border-white/5 pb-1">
          Abductive Causal Readout
        </h4>
        
        <!-- Factual Card -->
        <div class="p-3 mb-3 bg-[#141310] border border-white/5 rounded">
          <div class="flex justify-between items-center mb-1">
            <span class="text-[0.7rem] font-mono text-ink-dim uppercase">Factual World (M)</span>
            <span id="factual-badge" class="px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.6rem] font-mono rounded font-bold">...</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex justify-between items-baseline">
            <span class="text-[0.65rem] font-mono text-ink-dim">Y* = 2.0(T*) + 1.5(X) + U_Y</span>
            <span id="factual-y-val" class="font-mono text-sm text-ink font-bold">0.00</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Counterfactual Card -->
        <div class="p-3 bg-[#141310] border border-white/5 rounded">
          <div class="flex justify-between items-center mb-1">
            <span class="text-[0.7rem] font-mono text-ink-dim uppercase">Counterfactual World (M_x)</span>
            <span id="counterfactual-badge" class="px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.6rem] font-mono rounded font-bold">...</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex justify-between items-baseline">
            <span class="text-[0.65rem] font-mono text-ink-dim">Y_x = 2.0(T_c) + 1.5(X) + U_Y</span>
            <span id="counterfactual-y-val" class="font-mono text-sm text-ink font-bold">0.00</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Causal Effect Metric -->
      <div class="border-t border-white/5 pt-3">
        <div class="flex justify-between items-center">
          <span class="text-[0.65rem] font-mono uppercase text-ink-dim">Individual Treatment Effect (&tau;_i)</span>
          <span id="individual-effect-val" class="font-mono text-base font-bold text-accent">0.00</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-[0.6rem] font-mono text-ink-dim mt-1 leading-relaxed">
          The difference representing the exact value of the counterfactual intervention for this specific individual.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  
  <!-- Retrospective Narrative Console -->
  <div class="sandbox-console bg-[#09090a] border-t border-white/5 p-4 font-mono text-[0.72rem] text-code-txt rounded-b -mt-1 leading-relaxed">
    <div class="console-line flex justify-between mb-2 border-b border-dashed border-white/5 pb-2">
      <span>Causal Step: <span id="console-step" class="text-accent font-bold">Abduction &amp; Inference</span></span>
      <span>Shared Noise: <span class="text-stone-400">U_Y is fixed across worlds</span></span>
    </div>
    <div class="console-narrative text-accent text-[0.75rem] min-h-[3rem]" id="console-narrative-text">
      Adjust sliders to begin.
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
  function initCausalSandbox() {
    const sliderX = document.getElementById('confounder-x') as HTMLInputElement | null;
    const sliderT = document.getElementById('factual-t') as HTMLInputElement | null;
    const sliderUy = document.getElementById('exogenous-uy') as HTMLInputElement | null;
    const sliderTc = document.getElementById('counterfactual-tc') as HTMLInputElement | null;

    const valX = document.getElementById('val-x');
    const valT = document.getElementById('val-t');
    const valUy = document.getElementById('val-uy');
    const valTc = document.getElementById('val-tc');

    const factualYVal = document.getElementById('factual-y-val');
    const factualBadge = document.getElementById('factual-badge');
    const counterfactualYVal = document.getElementById('counterfactual-y-val');
    const counterfactualBadge = document.getElementById('counterfactual-badge');
    const individualEffectVal = document.getElementById('individual-effect-val');

    const consoleNarrative = document.getElementById('console-narrative-text');

    if (!sliderX || !sliderT || !sliderUy || !sliderTc || !valX || !valT || !valUy || !valTc || 
        !factualYVal || !factualBadge || !counterfactualYVal || !counterfactualBadge || 
        !individualEffectVal || !consoleNarrative) return;

    function update() {
      const X = parseFloat(sliderX!.value);
      const T = parseFloat(sliderT!.value);
      const Uy = parseFloat(sliderUy!.value);
      const Tc = parseFloat(sliderTc!.value);

      valX!.textContent = X.toFixed(2);
      valT!.textContent = T.toFixed(2);
      valUy!.textContent = Uy.toFixed(2);
      valTc!.textContent = Tc.toFixed(2);

      // Compute factual outcome Y*
      const Y_fact = 2.0 * T + 1.5 * X + Uy;
      factualYVal!.textContent = Y_fact.toFixed(4);

      // Compute counterfactual outcome Y_x
      const Y_counter = 2.0 * Tc + 1.5 * X + Uy;
      counterfactualYVal!.textContent = Y_counter.toFixed(4);

      // Compute ITE
      const ITE = Y_counter - Y_fact;
      individualEffectVal!.textContent = (ITE >= 0 ? '+' : '') + ITE.toFixed(4);

      // Factual status badge
      if (Y_fact >= 0) {
        factualBadge!.textContent = "SURVIVED";
        factualBadge!.className = "px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.6rem] font-mono rounded font-bold bg-emerald-950 text-emerald-400 border border-emerald-800/30";
      } else {
        factualBadge!.textContent = "FATAL COLLISION";
        factualBadge!.className = "px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.6rem] font-mono rounded font-bold bg-rose-950 text-rose-400 border border-rose-800/30";
      }

      // Counterfactual status badge
      if (Y_counter >= 0) {
        counterfactualBadge!.textContent = "SURVIVED (GHOST)";
        counterfactualBadge!.className = "px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.6rem] font-mono rounded font-bold bg-emerald-950 text-emerald-300 border border-emerald-700/40";
      } else {
        counterfactualBadge!.textContent = "FATAL (GHOST)";
        counterfactualBadge!.className = "px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.6rem] font-mono rounded font-bold bg-rose-950 text-rose-300 border border-rose-700/40";
      }

      // Narrative logic
      let narrative = "";
      if (Y_fact < 0 && Y_counter >= 0) {
        narrative = `RETROSPECTIVE JUSTICE: In the factual world, the passenger suffered a fatal injury (Y* = ${Y_fact.toFixed(2)}) under low braking (T* = ${T.toFixed(2)}). However, by abducting their unobserved resilience (U_Y = ${Uy.toFixed(2)}) and keeping it constant, we predict that they WOULD HAVE SURVIVED (Y_x = ${Y_counter.toFixed(2)}) had maximum braking been applied (T_c = ${Tc.toFixed(2)}). The intervention was causally decisive (ITE = +${ITE.toFixed(2)}).`;
      } else if (Y_fact >= 0 && Y_counter < 0) {
        narrative = `THE SWERVE TRAGEDY: In the factual world, the passenger survived (Y* = ${Y_fact.toFixed(2)}) under maximum braking (T* = ${T.toFixed(2)}). Had the vehicle switched to swerving (T_c = ${Tc.toFixed(2)}), the passenger WOULD HAVE DIED (Y_x = ${Y_counter.toFixed(2)}) despite their resilience. This proves that the automated braking system's factual decision was the but-for cause of their survival.`;
      } else if (Y_fact < 0 && Y_counter < 0) {
        narrative = `INEVITABLE LOSS: The collision is fatal in both worlds. Even under counterfactual intervention (T_c = ${Tc.toFixed(2)}), the poor visibility (X = ${X.toFixed(2)}) and low passenger resilience (U_Y = ${Uy.toFixed(2)}) make survival mathematically impossible (Y_x = ${Y_counter.toFixed(2)}). No human driver or software could have altered the outcome.`;
      } else {
        narrative = `ROBUST SURVIVAL: The passenger survives in both worlds. Their unobserved safety factor (U_Y = ${Uy.toFixed(2)}) and clear environmental contrast (X = ${X.toFixed(2)}) were sufficient to protect them, regardless of whether the system applied full braking or chose to swerve.`;
      }
      consoleNarrative!.textContent = narrative;
    }

    sliderX.addEventListener('input', update);
    sliderT.addEventListener('input', update);
    sliderUy.addEventListener('input', update);
    sliderTc.addEventListener('input', update);

    update();
  }

  // Initialize
  initCausalSandbox();
  document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', () => {
    initCausalSandbox();
  });
</script>
